// `@validated` channels literal construction and applies to a struct or a class. On an enum it is a
// misplacement (E0054). This reported NOTHING before the directive placement check was unified:
// `EnumDecl` had no `validated` field, so the parser discarded the directive and the author got
// silence — the program looked accepted.
// expect: error E0054 at 7:2
// expect: exit 1
@validated
enum Color { Red; Green }
echo "unreached"
